@startuml auth-flow
!theme plain
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam participantPadding 30
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 200
skinparam sequenceGroupBodyBackgroundColor transparent
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor       "User"          as U
participant "Angular App"   as A
participant "Keycloak"      as KC
participant "Spring Boot"   as API
database    "PostgreSQL"    as DB

== Login ==

U  ->  A  : Open app
|||
A  ->  KC : Redirect to /realms/ledgerview/login\n(PKCE authorization code flow)
|||
U  ->  KC : Submit credentials
KC ->  A  : Redirect with authorization code
|||
A  ->  KC : Exchange code for tokens
KC ->  A  : JWT access token (signed RS256)

|||
== Authenticated Request ==
|||

A  ->  API : GET /api/accounts\nAuthorization: Bearer <JWT>
|||
API -> KC  : Fetch JWKS (cached)\nVerify signature + claims
|||
API -> DB  : SELECT ... WHERE user_id = <sub from JWT>
DB  -> API : Result rows
API -> A   : 200 JSON response

|||
== Token Refresh ==
|||

A  ->  KC : POST /token  (refresh_token)
KC ->  A  : New access token

|||
== Dev Mode (unsecured profile) ==
|||

note over U, DB
  With "unsecured" Spring profile JWT validation is skipped.
  All requests treated as dev admin user (00000000-…-000001).
  Never use in production.
end note

@enduml
